{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>All these words.</b> This teaches that the Holy One, blessed be He, said all Ten Commandments in a single utterance, of which the mouth cannot speak. If so, why does it say ״אנכי״ and ״לא יהיה לך״? This teaches that Moses repeated each and every utterance on its own. Thus it is in the Sifra. And it is puzzling: what is difficult to him? If they were said in a single utterance, in any case Moses our master, peace be upon him, needed to say each and every one on its own. And one may answer: this is what was difficult to him — if they were said in a single utterance, why did Moses our master separate the cantillation signs? He should have said them all as one verse. And he answers: 'this teaches that he repeated,' etc. And Rabbi Baruch, of blessed memory, explained: 'if so, why does it say אנכי and לא יהיה לך?' — which implies that these alone He said, for in both of them there is one melody, as though the two of them are a single utterance, and they are also written in the language of the Holy One, blessed be He, as though He Himself is speaking: אנכי, הוצאתיך, על פני, לאוהבי — but the rest of the commandments each have a verse of its own, aside from לא תרצח, לא תנאף, לא תגנוב; and there is also a break between one and the other, and they are written in the language of Moses and not in the language of the Holy One, blessed be He. And that is what is said in tractate חגיגה: אנכי and לא יהיה לך we heard from the mouth of the Almighty. And he asks: 'if so, why does it say אנכי and לא יהיה לך?' — that is, did they not differ from the other commandments only in that all of them were said in a single utterance? And he answers: that he repeated each and every utterance on its own — but we heard from His mouth only two."], :book :exodus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :register {:flags {0 ["the Almighty"]}}, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:03:35.175074841Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}